From: Armada <no-reply@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: WFI in A722 binning when vertex buffers change

When the vertex buffer bindings change between draws in a render pass,
the A722's binning pass appears to bin a draw with the vertex buffers
of an earlier one. Geometry goes missing from some tiles and flickers,
and the GPU raises RBBM GPC errors (RBBM_INT_0 bit 7). It shows on
transparent effects and moving sprites drawn from a streamed vertex
buffer that is rebound between draws.

Rendering is correct in sysmem mode and in GMEM mode without binning.
Waiting for idle before every draw in the render pass fixes it.
Narrowing that down, only draws that change the vertex buffers need
the wait, and only in the binning pass: the same wait in the GMEM tile
passes alone leaves the flicker. With the wait in the binning pass, the
flicker and the GPC errors both stop.

Emit a WFI under a binning-only CP_COND_REG_EXEC before draws that
change the vertex buffers, on A722 only. TU_CMD_DIRTY_DRAW_STATE is
included because draws after a 3D clear re-enable the vertex buffer
draw state without TU_CMD_DIRTY_VERTEX_BUFFERS. The tile passes skip
the wait, and draws that keep their vertex buffers are unaffected.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h
index 18717e2..098d190 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h
@@ -442,6 +442,13 @@ struct fd_dev_info {
        */
       bool storage_ubwc_internal_quirk;
 
+      /* a722's binning pass appears to bin a draw with the vertex buffers
+       * of an earlier one when the bindings change between draws, which
+       * drops geometry from some bins and raises RBBM GPC errors. Wait for
+       * idle in the binning pass before draws that change them.
+       */
+      bool binning_vb_change_wfi_quirk;
+
       /* Whether CP_ALWAYS_ON_COUNTER only resets on device loss rather than
        * on every suspend/resume.
        */
diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
index 3ee309f..366e52d 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1123,7 +1123,8 @@ add_gpus([
         CHIP.A7XX,
         [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen1, GPUProps(no_bv = True,
                                         has_lpac = False,
-                                        storage_ubwc_internal_quirk = True)],
+                                        storage_ubwc_internal_quirk = True,
+                                        binning_vb_change_wfi_quirk = True)],
         num_ccu = 2,
         tile_align_w = 64,
         tile_align_h = 32,
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
index 50b33de..c967218 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
@@ -8682,6 +8682,18 @@ tu6_draw_common(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd,
 
    tu_emit_cache_flush_renderpass<CHIP>(cmd);
 
+   /* TU_CMD_DIRTY_DRAW_STATE re-enables the vertex buffer draw state
+    * after a 3D clear without setting TU_CMD_DIRTY_VERTEX_BUFFERS.
+    */
+   if ((cmd->state.dirty & (TU_CMD_DIRTY_VERTEX_BUFFERS |
+                            TU_CMD_DIRTY_DRAW_STATE)) &&
+       cmd->device->physical_device->info->props.binning_vb_change_wfi_quirk) {
+      tu_cond_exec_start(cs, CP_COND_REG_EXEC_0_MODE(RENDER_MODE) |
+                             CP_COND_REG_EXEC_0_BINNING);
+      tu_cs_emit_wfi(cs);
+      tu_cond_exec_end(cs);
+   }
+
   if (BITSET_TEST(cmd->vk.dynamic_graphics_state.dirty,
                   MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_IA_PRIMITIVE_RESTART_ENABLE) ||
       BITSET_TEST(cmd->vk.dynamic_graphics_state.dirty,
